          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Grothendieck65"} Grothendieck 1965
            understood
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            as locally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            over a fixed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            whose objects are interpreted as local models (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+geometry"}> functorial geometry
            ”). If local models are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+spaces"} algebraic spaces
            can be considered as an example.
          %h2#SchemesAsPresheaves Schemes as presheaves
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+ring"} ground ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Scheme
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Scheme
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
            (over
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+topological+spaces"} locally ringed topological spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aff
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Scheme
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff \hookrightarrow Scheme
            denote its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
          %p
            The assgnment which takes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Scheme
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \in Scheme
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+ring"} spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(-)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+sections"} global sections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_Y(-)
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_Y
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Y
                  \\mapsto
                  Spec\big(
                  \\Gamma_Y (\mathcal{O}_Y)
                  \\big)
          %p
            extends to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Scheme
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Aff
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Scheme \longrightarrow Aff
                  \\,.
          %p
            A basic result, sometimes referred to as the
            = succeed "," do
              %strong fundamental theorem on morphisms of schemes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CRing
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi Y
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≅
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Scheme
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CRing\big(R, \Gamma_Y\mathcal{O}_Y\big)
                  \\;\cong\;
                  Scheme(Y, Spec R).
          %p
            More precisely, for a fixed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction"} restriction
            functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Scheme
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Aff
                        %mi op
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Aff
                        %mi op
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi CRing
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi CRing
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Set
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Scheme(-,Y)\vert_{Aff^{op}}
                  \\;=\;
                  h_Y|_{Aff^{op}}
                  \\;=\;
                  h_Y|_{CRing}
                  \\,\colon\,
                  CRing \longrightarrow Set
                  \\,,
          %p and the functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi CRing
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Y
                  \\,\mapsto\,
                  h_Y|_{CRing}
          %p
            from schemes to presheaves on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aff
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi CRing
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff = CRing^{op}
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+spaces"} ringed spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff
          %p
            In fact, the theorem is more general: instead of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            being a scheme, we can take any locally ringed space. Thus the entire category of locally ringed spaces embeds into the category of presheaves on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff
          %h2#schemes_as_locally_representable_sheaves Schemes as locally representable sheaves
          %p
            One can characterize the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+image"} essential image
            of the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
            in the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            over the category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            spanned by those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+presheaves"} small presheaves
            that are
            = succeed "-locally" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            = succeed "-sheaves," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+topology"} Zariski topology
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff
          %p
            More precisely, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AffSch
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi CRing
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AffSch \coloneqq CRing^{op}
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
            but now defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            of that of commutative (unital) rings. Define the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+topology"} Zariski topology
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AffSch
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AffSch
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            generated by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
            given by families
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{Spec R[r^{-1}] \to Spec R\mid r\in R\}
          %p
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi AffSch
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\in AffSch
          %p
            Now consider the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+sheaves"} small sheaves
            on the site
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi AffSch
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AffSch
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+presheaves"} small presheaves
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AffSch
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AffSch
            that satisfy the gluing property with respect to every covering family in the coverage.
          %p
            A presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is
            %strong locally representable
            if there is a set-indexed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+family"} covering family
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i\colon X_i\to F,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
            is the representable sheaf of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine scheme
            and the morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+immersions"} open immersions
          %p Open immersions of presheaves are defined as follows. A morphism of presheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\to G
          %p
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+immersion"} open immersion
            if for every presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            represented by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine scheme
            and every morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to G,
          %p
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times_G F\to X
          %p
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+immersion"} open immersion
          %p
            See
            %a{:href => "#DemazureGabriel70"} Demazure &amp; Gabriel 1970
            for the functorial approach to schemes and its relation to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+spaces"} locally ringed spaces
          %h2#noncommutative_analogues Noncommutative analogues
          %p
            See
            %a{:href => "#R1998"} Rosenberg 1998
            for fundamental theorem on morphisms, and 1999 for the equivalence of two approaches)
          %h2#derived_analogues Derived analogues
          %p …(Toen, Vezzosi etc.)
          %h2#references References
          %h3#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"}> affine scheme
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+scheme"} algebraic scheme
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+schemes"} morphism of schemes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"}> Yoneda embedding
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} Isbell duality
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+geometry"} functorial geometry
          %h2#literature Literature
          %p
            The original observation (cf.
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+geometry"} functorial geometry
          %ul
            %li#Grothendieck65
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction au langage fonctoriel
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Karoubi"} Max Karoubi
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~leila.schneps/grothendieckcircle/GrothAlgiers.pdf"}> pdf scan
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GrothendieckIntroductionLangageFonctoriel1965.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Grothendieck73
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to functorial algebraic geometry, part 1: affine algebraic geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://matematicas.unex.es/~navarro/res/ifag.pdf"} pdf scan
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GrothendieckIntrodFunctorialGeometryI1973.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#DemazureGabriel70
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michel+Demazure"}> Michel Demazure
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Gabriel"} Pierre Gabriel
              = succeed "," do
                %em Groupes algebriques
              %em Corps de classes local
              par
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michiel+Hazewinkel"} Hazewinkel M
          %p English translation:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michel+Demazure"}> Michel Demazure
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Gabriel"} Peter Gabriel
              = succeed "," do
                %em Introduction to algebraic geometry and algebraic groups
              %strong 39
              (1980) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://shop.elsevier.com/books/introduction-to-algebraic-geometry-and-algebraic-groups/demazure/978-0-444-85443-8"}> ISBN:9780080871509
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            See also the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MathOverflow"} MathOverflow
            answer:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zhen+Lin+Low"}> Zhen Lin Low
              \:
              %em Answer to “What is a (Zariski-)locally representable (pre)sheaf?”
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/491645/381"}> MO:a/491645
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            For the fundamental theorem of morphisms of schemes in the language of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+spaces"} locally ringed spaces
            see for example Theorem 2 in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kiran+Kedlaya"}> Kiran Kedlaya
              \:
              %em Morphisms of Schemes
              Lectures 7–9 in
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic Geometry
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-726-algebraic-geometry-spring-2009/resources/mit18_726s09_lec06_morphisms"} pdf
          %p
            The fundamental theorem of morphisms of schemes has been adapted to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+schemes"} noncommutative schemes
            in
          %ul
            %li#R1998
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"}> Alexander Rosenberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Noncommutative schemes
              %strong 112
              (1998) 93–125
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1000479824211"} doi
        .revisedby
